9	Dont use String,int and char literals in the java classes.Move them in to common initerface.

	Eg:
	
		String name="merchant"; /* Dont use string literal like this*/
		
		String name=LiteralConstants.NAME; /* Use like this*/
		
10 	Dont declare any variable in loop.Create instance outside of the loop and use it.

	Eg:
			/*This is wrong*/
			for(int i=0;i<10;i++){
				String sample = List.get(i);
			}

			/*This is fine*/
			String sample=LiteralConstans.EMPTYSTRING ;/*assigning empty string*/
			for(int i=0;i<10;i++){
				sample = List.get(i);
			}
			
11  Dont use strings when the concatenation is done.This will create lot of instances  and consumes memory.Use stringBuffer .

	Eg	:	
			/*This is not fine*/
			String s="sample";
			s=s+"end";
			
			/*This is fine*/
			StringBuffer s=new StringBuffer("sample");
			s.append("end");

12 Avoid condition checkings in if loop like below....

	Eg:		
			/*This is not fine*/
			if(s!=null){
				if(s.equals("one)){
				/* code*/
				}
			}	
	
			/*This is fine*/
			if( s!=null && s.equals("one) ){
			/*code*/
			} 
			
13	 Cleanup the objects when  the objects are no more need.Close database connections,resultsets and statements properly.


14	Use log.trace() at starting and ending of the method.  Use log.debug()  when you want to log some inofmrations. Use log.fatal() when the applicaion throws severe exception. log.error() when the application throws particular defined exception.

	Eg :
	
			private List searchResult(String sqlCount_Query, String sqlSearch_Query, String strSQL, List paramList, int maxRecord) throws DAOException,BillRegAppException {
			List merchantSearchLst = null;
				if (log.isTraceEnabled()) {
					log.trace(MethodNames.SEARCHRESULT + LiteralConstants.METHODSTART);
				}
				/*		 Execute the Query to find out record count for this particular search option */
			
				merchantSearchLst = (List) executePSQuery(sqlCount_Query + LiteralConstants.EMPTYSPACE + strSQL, paramList);
				if (merchantSearchLst != null) {
					String[] strNoRecord = (String[]) merchantSearchLst.get(0);
					/*
					* If the Record Cound is greater than displayed search record (XML
					* read value), throw user define exception.
					*/
			
					if (strNoRecord != null && Integer.parseInt(strNoRecord[0]) > maxRecord) {
						BillRegAppException billRegExp = new BillRegAppException(ErrorConstants.APP_MORERECORD,
							"Number of returned records is greater than [Actual limit] -  " + maxRecord);
						if (log.isErrorEnabled()) {
							log.error(LiteralConstants.ERROR, billRegExp);
						}
						throw billRegExp;
					} else if (strNoRecord != null) {
					/*
						* Execute the Query to fetch the search criteria values.
						*/
					merchantSearchLst = (List) executePSQuery(sqlSearch_Query + LiteralConstants.EMPTYSPACE + strSQL, paramList);
					}
				}
			if (log.isTraceEnabled()) {
				log.trace(MethodNames.SEARCHRESULT + LiteralConstants.METHODEND);
			}
			return merchantSearchLst;
			}

11	Number of lines in a class should not be greater than 1000. Number of lines in one method should not be greater than 100. single line length should not be geater than 80 characters.

12 	Use variable names as reasonable with naming convention. Avoid abbreviations whenever there is better words to use. Use capital letters for constant variables.

		Eg :
				Naming Conventions

						packages
							lowercase.
							Consider using the recommended domain-based conventions described in the Java Language Specification, page 107 as prefixes. (For example, EDU.oswego.cs.dl.) 
						
						files
							The java compiler enforces the convention that file names have the same base name as the public class they define. 
						
						classes:
							CapitalizedWithInternalWordsAlsoCapitalized 
						
						Exception class:
							ClassNameEndsWithException. 
						
						Interface. When necessary to distinguish from similarly named classes:
							InterfaceNameEndsWithIfc. 
						
						Class. When necessary to distinguish from similarly named interfaces:
							ClassNameEndsWithImpl OR 
							ClassNameEndsWithObject 
						
						constants (finals):
							UPPER_CASE_WITH_UNDERSCORES 
						
						private or protected: (pick one!)
							firstWordLowerCaseButInternalWordsCapitalized OR 
							trailingUnderscore_, OR 
							thisVar (i.e. prefix with this), OR 
							myVar (i.e. prefix with my), OR 
							fVar (i.e. prefix with f)
						
						static private or protected:
							firstWordLowerCaseButInternalWordsCapitalized OR 
							twoTrailingUnderscores__ 
						
						local variables:
							firstWordLowerCaseButInternalWordsCapitalized OR 
							lower_case_with_underscores 
						
						methods:
							firstWordLowerCaseButInternalWordsCapitalized() 
							factory method for objects of type X:
							newX 
						
						converter method that returns objects of type X:
							toX 
						
						method that reports an attribute x of type X:
							X x() or X getX(). 
						
						method that changes an attribute x of type X:
							void x(X value) or void setX(X value). 


	

13  If the action class needs session variable use it as local  private variable . Remove the session variable when the that variable's scope is over.

14. Dont use java scriptlet in JSP pages. use struts  framework tags.

15 Move common javascript functions to common JS file. Give necessary comments in javaScript methods.

16.	Dont hardcode page contents in JSP file. Use ApplicationReaources.properties file.

17.	Avoid conditional operators. It makes the code harder to understand.

18.	Avoid calling same function again and again in a method. Assign the returning variable in to local variable and use it. Calling functions so much time increaces the memory stack.

		Eg:
				/* this is not fine*/
				if( merchantForm.getUserId()!=null &&  merchantForm.getUserId().equals("ebo")){
					pageBean.setUserId(merchantForm.getUserId());
				}
				
				/*this is fine*/
				String userId = merchantForm.getUserId();
				if( userId!=null &&  userId.equals("ebo")){
					pageBean.setUserId(userId);
				}

				
19.	 Avoid using the same name as the incoming parameter. Assign into a local variable and use it.

		Eg:
				/* This is not fine*/
				public String sampleMethod(String userId){
					
					if(userId.equals("1")){
						userId="2";
					}
					return userId;
				}


				/* This is fine*/
				public String sampleMethod(String userId){
					String localUserId=userId;
					if(localUserId.equals("1")){
						localUserId="2";
					}
					return localUserId;
				}
				
20	Avoid using StringTokenizer. use Split API.


21.	Dont import Classes using *. Import individual classes which the code wants. 

		Eg :	
				/* Avoid This*/
				import org.apache.commons.logging.*;

				/* This is OK*/
				import org.apache.commons.logging.Log;
	
				
